---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Corporate Fitness and Wellness Programs';
const description = 'Corporate fitness and wellness programs that combine movement, recovery, nutrition, ergonomics and mental performance for healthier teams.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Corporate Wellness</div><h1>Corporate fitness and wellness programs for healthier, more consistent teams.</h1><p class="lead">Workplace wellness works best when it is simple, repeatable and built around real human behavior. A strong program should support movement, recovery, nutrition, stress management and practical education employees can actually use.</p></div></section>
<section class="content"><div class="container"><article>

<h2>What corporate fitness and wellness should include</h2><p>A good workplace wellness program should be more than a gym discount or a one-time challenge. Employees need realistic tools that fit into the workday, support long-term habits and help them feel better physically and mentally.</p><ul><li>Short guided workouts for different ability levels.</li><li>Mobility and body care routines for desk workers and active employees.</li><li>Nutrition education focused on energy, protein, hydration and recovery.</li><li>Mental performance tools such as breathing, reflection and body awareness.</li><li>Ergonomics guidance for remote, hybrid and office teams.</li></ul><h2>Why companies invest in employee wellness</h2><p>Teams often struggle with stress, fatigue, inconsistent movement, low energy and aches from sitting. A structured wellness app gives employees one place to build better routines without needing a complicated program.</p><h2>Best-fit use cases</h2><p>This type of program can work for corporate offices, remote teams, schools, athletic departments, healthcare teams, first responders and organizations that want practical wellness support.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Content angle:</strong> This page should connect the topic back to the app naturally. Mention guided training, body care, nutrition education and mental performance where relevant without forcing a sales pitch.</div>
</article></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
